{
  "body_human_readable": "In 2024, Tesla sold approximately 1.79 million vehicles globally. This marked the company's first annual sales decline in 12 years, representing a 1.1% decrease from the 1.81 million vehicles sold in 2023.\n\nThe total number of vehicles delivered in 2024 was 1,789,226. During the same period, Tesla produced 1,773,443 vehicles.\n\nHere's a breakdown of deliveries by quarter in 2024:\n*   **First Quarter:** 386,810 vehicles\n*   **Fourth Quarter:** Over 495,000 vehicles\n\nThe Tesla Model Y continued to be the best-selling electric vehicle in the United States in 2024, with 372,613 units sold. The Tesla Model 3 followed with 189,903 sales in the US.\n\nDespite the slight dip in sales, Tesla's revenue for 2024 was $97.7 billion, a slight increase from the previous year.",
